     "count": 1,
     "explain": "NPUWattch assumes that each block is clock-gated, thus an idle cycle costs no dynamic energy. A register-file or FIFO access costs its mode energy minus the idle energy, because a gated array clocks only the accessed row. A datapath event is one active cycle and costs its full energy. To model a block without clock gating, set clock_gating: false on its component."
